          "---\nname: agent-ui\ndescription:\n  Use when building or changing the homepage agent-review demo in apps/docs, its\n  mock-data generator, the Conductor-style diff/changes layout, or editable\n  diffs wiring @pierre/diffs FileDiff with @pierre/trees FileTree in the Next.js\n  docs app.\n---\n\n# Agent UI (homepage demo)\n\nA Conductor-style agent-review card embedded on the diffs homepage (the first\nsection below the hero). It frames the editor as an agent window: a center\neditable diff viewer (`@pierre/diffs`) and a right changed-files panel\n(`@pierre/trees`). All data is canned, so it runs on Vercel without runtime\nfilesystem/git access. There is no standalone route — the component is only\nrendered as a homepage section.\n\nThe demo is intentionally self-referential: the single live session, \"Add\nagent-review demo\", shows the actual source files the demo is built from.\n\n## Files\n\n- `apps/docs/app/(diffs)/_home/AgentUi.tsx` — `'use client'`. The interactive\n  component (`AgentUi`). Wraps the diff surface in `EditorProvider`, renders the\n  breadcrumb, the editable `FileDiff`, the static composer, and the right\n  `ChangesTree`. Theme is controlled by the parent via the `themeType` prop.\n- `apps/docs/app/(diffs)/_home/AgentDemoSection.tsx` — `'use client'`. The\n  homepage section wrapper: `FeatureHeader`, an icon-only light/dark\n  `ButtonGroup` (defaults the card to dark), and `<AgentUi />`.\n- `apps/docs/app/(diffs)/_home/Home.tsx` — `AgentReviewSection` is an async\n  server component that SSR-prerenders each changed file's diff\n  (`preloadFileDiff`, dark theme) and passes them to `AgentDemoSection` as\n  `prerenderedDiffs`.\n- `apps/docs/app/(diffs)/_home/mockData.ts` — `AuiSession` / `AuiChangedFile`\n  types, derive helpers (`getSessionPaths`, `getSessionDirectoryPaths`,\n  `getSessionGitStatus`, `getFileDiff`), and the exported `AUI_SESSIONS`.\n- `apps/docs/app/(diffs)/_home/mockData.generated.ts` — AUTO-GENERATED snapshot\n  of real repo file contents. Do not edit by hand.\n- `apps/docs/scripts/generate-aui-mock-data.ts` — bun + git generator that\n  writes `mockData.generated.ts`.\n- `apps/docs/app/(diffs)/_home/agent-ui.css` — all chrome, scoped under `.aui`\n  so it never leaks into the rest of the docs app.\n\n## Mock data\n\nRegenerate the snapshot from the live repo:\n\n```bash\nbun apps/docs/scripts/generate-aui-mock-data.ts\n```\n\nThe generator enumerates `SELF_SESSION_FILES` (the demo's source files,\nexcluding the generated blob itself). For each file: `after` = on-disk contents,\n`before` = `git show HEAD:<path>` (or `''` if new), `status` = `added` |\n`modified`, and `additions`/`deletions` from `git diff --numstat HEAD` (falling\nback to a line count for untracked new files). It is a committed snapshot —\ndrift over time is acceptable; re-run to refresh.\n\n## Editable diffs\n\n- Worker pool: the homepage provides a shared `WorkerPoolContext` (see\n  `_components/WorkerPoolContext.tsx`) initialized with `DEFAULT_THEMES` and\n  `useTokenTransformer: true` (required for editing). `AgentUi` defaults its\n  `theme` prop to `DEFAULT_THEMES` to match that pool.\n- The center surface is the React `FileDiff` with `contentEditable` inside\n  `EditorProvider`, which auto-attaches the editor. It is keyed by the active\n  path so it remounts when the file changes. Options: `disableFileHeader`,\n  `overflow: 'wrap'`, `diffStyle: 'unified'`.\n- `getFileDiff(file, nextAfter)` builds `FileDiffMetadata` via\n  `parseDiffFromFile(before, after)`. Edits are persisted in a ref keyed by path\n  (the editor's debounced `onChange` has no path arg, so the live target is\n  tracked in `activeTargetRef`), so switching files keeps the agent's tweaked\n  output.\n- SSR: `AgentUi` reuses `prerenderedDiffs[path]` as `prerenderedHTML` only while\n  the demo is in dark mode (the snapshot is dark) and the file is unedited, so\n  the card paints highlighted on first load and hydrates cleanly.\n- Line numbers: the editor stylesheet flattens line-number colour to one neutral\n  value (and is unlayered, so it beats the library's `@layer base` per-line\n  colours). `AgentUi` adopts an extra higher-specificity sheet into the diff's\n  shadow root to restore jade/red numbers for added/deleted lines.\n- Changed-files tree: `ChangesTree` creates an imperative `@pierre/trees`\n  `FileTree` in an effect (recreated per session), seeded fully expanded via\n  `initialExpandedPaths`, with `gitStatus` colours and per-row `+adds −dels` via\n  `renderRowDecoration` (jade/red, zero counts hidden). Selecting a file swaps\n  the active surface; the active file is mirrored back into the tree selection.\n\n## Theme\n\nSelf-contained light/dark toggle lives in `AgentDemoSection` (defaults to dark)\nand is passed into `AgentUi` via `themeType`. On the `.aui` root,\n`data-theme-type` pins `color-scheme`; the tree's `:host { color-scheme }` is\noverridden by setting the container's inline `style.colorScheme`. It never\ntouches the docs `<html>` theme.\n\n## Layout\n\n`.aui` is a fixed-height card (taller on `width >= 1024px`). The body is a\ntwo-column grid (diff + 380px changes panel). On `width < 640px` the changes\nsidebar is hidden and the diff goes full-width (single-file view).\n\n## Static chrome\n\nThe composer (textarea + Agent/Mythos selectors + send) and the All files /\nChecks tabs are non-functional, present only for screenshot fidelity.\n\n## Verification\n\nFrom the repo root: `bun run format`, `bun run lint`, `bun run lint:css`. From\n`apps/docs`: `bun run tsc`. Then load the homepage and check file select, inline\nediting, the theme toggle, and the mobile single-file layout.\n",
